"**Where it was said.** In Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī, ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ said: “I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb on the pulpit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Actions are only by intentions…’” ʿUmar chose to announce it publicly to the people, showing how important it is.",
"**The story of ‘the Emigrant of Umm Qays’.** ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: “There was a man among us who proposed to a woman called Umm Qays. She refused to marry him unless he emigrated, so he emigrated and married her, and we used to call him ‘the Emigrant of Umm Qays’.” This story is authentic: aṭ-Ṭabarānī recorded it, and Ibn Ḥajar said its chain is authentic by the standards of al-Bukhārī and Muslim.",
